%% Chart to release — Packaging & Distributing Your App.
%% Step 1 of the SA demo: what `helm install` actually does, left to right — one values file drives
%% the rendered manifests, the install records a release revision, and the release is a running Pod
%% behind a browsable edge Route. Authored 2026-09-12 because the two summary diagrams this module
%% already ships (03-what-you-built, 04-platform-accretion) recap the WHOLE module; a customer reads
%% the picture before the words, so a step needs a picture of that step.
%% ---
%% Deliberately flat: a five-node LR chain with NO subgraph. A subgraph that declares `direction`
%% and has any edge crossing its boundary has that `direction` silently discarded (see the sibling
%% 02-olm-anatomy.mmd header for the measurements), and there is nothing here worth that risk.
%% ---
%% NEVER put an angle-bracket placeholder in a .mmd file. Antora emits mermaid source into the page
%% UNESCAPED, so a word wrapped in angle brackets becomes a REAL DOM element that swallows the rest
%% of the graph; the line-break tag is the only markup safe inside a label. Write placeholders in
%% CAPS. Second trap, same symptom: a BARE "%%" line with no text after it defeats mermaid's comment
%% stripper and the diagram dies the same silent way — always put text after %%, as "%% ---" does.
graph LR
  v["values.yaml<br/>image · port 8080 · /health"] --> t["rendered manifests<br/>Deployment · Service · Route"] --> i["helm install<br/>release revision 1"] --> p["Pod Ready 1/1<br/>probes passing"] --> r["edge Route<br/>a URL in the browser"]
  classDef authored fill:#e8eaf6,stroke:#3949ab,color:#1a237e;
  classDef release fill:#fef7e0,stroke:#b06000,color:#7a4100;
  classDef running fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#137333,color:#0d652d;
  class v,t authored; class i release; class p,r running;
